<title>UK: Lonrho has no comment on EU probe report.</title>
<headline>Lonrho has no comment on EU probe report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lonrho Plc said it could not comment on a report that the European Commission was expected to launch a four-month probe into Anglo American's stake in the British group.</p>
<p>A spokesman said he could not discuss the report -- which cited an unnamed industry source -- as Lonrho would be subject rather than player in any probe.</p>
<p>Anglo-American recently raised its holding in Lonrho to 28 percent, making it the biggest shareholder by far.</p>
<p>This created competition problems as Anglo and Lonrho are both major miners of platinum.</p>
<p>Platinum is a precious metal used in jewellery and in car catalysts to clean exhaust fumes.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
